# AgriYield – Dataset Data Dictionary

## Dataset Information
- **Source:** FAOSTAT – Crops and Livestock Products
- **Country:** Rwanda
- **Records:** 234
- **Columns:** 15
- **Crops:** 6
- **Period:** 2010–2024 
- **File:** FAOSTAT_data_en_11-13-2026.csv

## Dataset Fields

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| Domain Code | FAOSTAT dataset identifier |
| Domain | Agricultural data category |
| Area Code (M49) | Country identification code |
| Area | Country name |
| Element Code | Indicator identification code |
| Element | Area harvested, Yield, or Production |
| Item Code (CPC) | Crop identification code |
| Item | Crop name |
| Year Code | Year identifier |
| Year | Observation year |
| Unit | Measurement unit |
| Value | Recorded agricultural value |
| Flag | Data quality/status code |
| Flag Description | Explanation of the data flag |
| Note | Additional information, if available |

## Main Indicators

- **Area harvested:** Measured in hectares (ha).
- **Yield:** Measured in hectograms per hectare (hg/ha).
- **Production:** Measured in tonnes (t).

## Data Quality
The dataset contains:
- 208 official values.
- 19 estimated values.
- 7 imputed values.

The original data-quality flags must be preserved during database import.

## Database Preparation Plan
1. Import the original CSV into a staging table.
2. Create crop records in the CROPS table.
3. Organize agricultural observations by crop and year.
4. Transform the three indicators into structured crop statistics.
5. Validate imported records against the original dataset.

## Data Limitation
The dataset contains historical country-level statistics for Rwanda. It does not provide individual farm-level production records. The years 2017 and 2018 are not represented in the downloaded file.
